f 17592186173035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172208 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186173036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172208 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186173102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172208 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186173103 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172208 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172208 #edb/ref 1045 "Further Rules of Absolute Value" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172208 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186173015 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172208 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172208 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172208 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "0db9f058-2c2b-5d1f-a85c-11f1e1e699e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172867 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186173102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172867 #edb/ref 1061 25123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172867 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4c2ee3dc-ab94-51f0-bcdc-ab20413c5355" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172867 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186172015 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173015 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186172867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173015 #edb/ref 1061 36685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173015 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "de7a2169-7d86-5d52-813f-d1d199541882" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173015 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186173210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173035 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186173103 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173035 #edb/ref 1061 3977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173035 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a35c659d-3a92-5292-a856-8e051b0df01d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173035 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186172111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173036 #edb/ref 1061 3978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173036 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6c3441ba-31e5-52c4-9a8b-3e8a4cd3a43d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173036 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186172112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173102 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186173035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173102 #edb/ref 1061 5019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173102 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f329f688-b5f5-5222-a1c0-599debe7606f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173102 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186173140 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173103 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186173036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173103 #edb/ref 1061 5922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173103 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3819c50d-8c6b-5e33-b8c9-e35bd4855c00" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173103 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186173141 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173140 #edb/ref 1064 "We know that the absolute value operation does nothing to a number if it is non-negative. For example:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|0| & =0 \\\\ |1| & =1 \\\\ |2| & =2 \\\\ |3| & =3 \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can summarize this fact as follows:\n\n$$\n|x| = x \\quad \\text{ if } \\quad x \\geq 0\n$$\n\nWe also know that $x^2$ is non-negative for any value of $x$. Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\left|x^2\\right| = x^2\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is *any* real number." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173140 #edb/ref 1065 1716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173140 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b20a7fe3-4627-5ed7-a7dd-afd383fa3c59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173140 #edb/ref 1067 "The Absolute Value of a Square" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173141 #edb/ref 1064 "We know that $|x|=x$ if $x \\geq 0.$ But what if $x < 0?$\n\nIf a variable is known to be negative, then the absolute value changes it to positive. To turn a negative number into a positive number, we multiply by $-1.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n|x|  = -x \\quad\\textrm{for}\\quad x < 0.\n$$\n\nTo convince ourselves that this is indeed true, let's verify it in the case when $x=-2.$ Substituting this value into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|-2| & =-(-2)=2.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173141 #edb/ref 1065 1831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173141 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "93c4f77c-611c-5870-88b3-e76b8bbc7275" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173141 #edb/ref 1067 "The Absolute Value of a Negative Variable" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173210 #edb/ref 1064 "In this lesson, we'll extend our knowledge of absolute value. \n\nLet's first remind ourselves of the rules of absolute value:\n\n- $|{-a}| = |a|$\n\n- $|a \\cdot b| = |a| \\cdot |b|$\n\n- $\\left| \\dfrac{a}{b} \\right| = \\dfrac{|a|}{|b|}$\n\nRecall that the last two rules are known as the **distributive properties.**" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173210 #edb/ref 1065 6010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173210 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3d23d2e9-6bc0-5a8b-bdb3-84a2f0e9d4d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173210 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489511 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186490338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489511 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186490343 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489511 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186490366 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489511 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489511 #edb/ref 1045 "Evaluating Expressions With Integer Exponents" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489511 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186490338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489511 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489511 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489511 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "dbf71e83-e6c5-5f76-a850-bb5e63425c3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489714 #edb/ref 1080 "-8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489714 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489714 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "545f6b34-8b08-5486-9f0e-2cc84dac10e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489731 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489731 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489731 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5923c943-f43e-5441-819c-fc4c38287552" #edb/ref 